# Icons — do not invent or generate

Inline UI icons are defined in:

- [`app/utils/icons-framework.js`](app/utils/icons-framework.js) — framework catalogue (`FRAMEWORK_ICONS`; synced / hashed)
- [`app/utils/icons-app.js`](app/utils/icons-app.js) — fork / app icons (`APP_ICONS`; never overwritten by sync)
- [`app/utils/icons.js`](app/utils/icons.js) — merges both (app wins on key clash) and exports `createIcon` / `initIcons`

See the **Available** lists in the framework catalogue and app file headers.

## Never

- Invent, guess, or generate SVG path data (`d="…"`, `<path>`, `<svg>`, etc.)
- Paste icon markup from memory, a casual web scrape, or image generation into HTML, CSS, or JS
- Duplicate SVG paths outside the icons modules above
- Approximate or “fix up” path `d` data when sourcing from Icônes

## When an icon is missing

1. **Stop** — do not substitute a made-up icon.
2. **Reuse** an existing icon if one is close enough (`data-icon`, `createIcon()`, or `{ ref: "other-icon" }`).
3. **Pull from Icônes** via the [`add-icon`](../skills/add-icon/SKILL.md) skill (Iconify fetch script — exact markup, `name`, and `attribution`). Prefer [Material Icons Round (`ic`)](https://icones.js.org/collection/ic?s=info&variant=Round); fall back to Material Symbols Rounded. Ask for the app id and place (framework catalogue vs app) if the user did not provide them.
4. Or ask the user to supply their own vector asset / paste markup — then use [`handle-assets`](../skills/handle-assets/SKILL.md) for stubs and wiring.
5. You may add a **blank placeholder entry** in `APP_ICONS` / `FRAMEWORK_ICONS` using the entry stub in those files (empty `markup`, correct `viewBox`) so wiring (`data-icon`, imports) can land in the same change — then tell the user to fill in the paths (or finish with `add-icon`).

## Allowed without user-provided paths

- `data-icon="existing-id"` / `createIcon("existing-id")` for ids already in the merged `ICONS`
- `{ ref: "existing-id" }` aliases
- Exact Iconify bodies inserted by following **`add-icon`** (fetch script only — not from memory)
- Blank icon stub with `markup: \`\`` only when the user has agreed to add the icon

## Logo / raster assets

Brand images stay in `app/res/` — same rule: do not invent; use existing files or ask the user to supply them.
